=== 4. sqrt(n)*L_n is n-independent? ===
sqrt(n)*L_n = sqrt(pi)/(2*sqrt(g))  (must have NO n left -- this is (sqrt(pi)/2)/sqrt(g))
Confirmed n-independent. (Earlier hand-check mistakenly used n*L_n instead of sqrt(n)*L_n -- n*L_n is NOT constant, it is Theta(sqrt(n)); sqrt(n)*L_n IS the n-independent quantity used implicitly by the proof's D-normalization. This distinction is worth stating explicitly since it's easy to get backwards.)

